    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "GPT5m chose to play Silverbluff Bridge (which enters tapped) instead of Island (which enters untapped). On turn 1, the hand contains Mind Stone (2 mana) and Oni-Cult Anvil (2 mana) as potential turn 2 plays. Playing Island now would allow casting Mind Stone on turn 2 with Island + Silverbluff Bridge (played turn 2 tapped), but actually either way Silverbluff Bridge enters tapped so the turn 2 sequencing matters. If you play Island turn 1, then Silverbluff Bridge turn 2 (tapped), you have 1 untapped mana on turn 2. If you play Silverbluff Bridge turn 1 (tapped), then Island turn 2, you have 2 untapped mana on turn 2 and can cast Mind Stone or Oni-Cult Anvil. Wait - re-reading: the 'After' line says 'puts Island from hand onto the Battlefield' which suggests Island was actually played despite choosing Silverbluff Bridge. But taking the choice at face value - choosing Silverbluff Bridge turn 1 means it untaps turn 2, then playing Island turn 2 gives 2 mana for Mind Stone. If Island were played turn 1, then Silverbluff Bridge turn 2 (tapped), only 1 untapped mana on turn 2. So actually Silverbluff Bridge first is correct for curving into a 2-drop on turn 2. This is the right play.",
      "action_taken": "Played Silverbluff Bridge (enters tapped) on turn 1",
      "better_line": "Actually this was correct - playing the tapped land first enables a 2-drop on turn 2",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 21,
      "player": "GPT5m Romance",
      "decision_index": 20,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Optim's commander is Aminatou, the Fateshifter (WUB colors), and they have both Dimir Signet (produces UB) and Azorius Signet (produces WU) available. With a Plains and Sejiri Refuge (W or U) already on the battlefield, plus Tranquil Cove (W or U) and Isolated Watchtower (C) in hand, their color coverage is heavily skewed toward W and U. Casting Azorius Signet would give them early access to WU (which they already have from lands), while Dimir Signet gives UB. Since they need B for Aminatou (which costs WUB) and have no black source yet, Dimir Signet is actually the correct choice to shore up the missing color. However, looking more carefully: they need W, U, AND B for Aminatou on turn 3. With Plains + Sejiri Refuge they have W and U covered. Dimir Signet (activated with 1 generic + tap = UB) gives them B access, which is correct. Azorius Signet would give WU which is redundant. So Dimir Signet is actually the right call here.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Dimir Signet",
      "better_line": "Dimir Signet was actually correct to enable casting Aminatou (WUB) by providing the missing black mana",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 35,
      "player": "Gem3F Optim",
      "decision_index": 28,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Halimar Depths lets you order the top 3 cards of your library. With Sol Ring and Puresteel Paladin as the two cards being ordered (the third was already placed), putting Sol Ring on top means drawing it next turn. However, GLM47 has Ebony Fly (2 mana artifact) in hand and could play Sol Ring turn 3 to accelerate into bigger plays. But Puresteel Paladin on top would be drawn turn 3, and with Sol Ring already in hand or on the field, Puresteel Paladin enables free equips and card draw from equipment entering. The key issue is that putting Sol Ring on top (drawing it next) delays Puresteel Paladin. Sol Ring is generally the stronger card to have early for mana acceleration, but looking at the hand: they have Abundant Growth (1 mana, draws a card), Fertile Ground (2 mana), Ebony Fly (2 mana), and expensive cards like Argentum Armor (6 mana) and Angel of Finality (4 mana). Sol Ring on top is actually very reasonable for mana acceleration. However, Puresteel Paladin on top would let them play it turn 3 (they have WW available potentially with lands + Fertile Ground/Abundant Growth), and then when Argentum Armor enters later, they draw a card and can equip for free with metalcraft. This is close enough that Sol Ring on top is defensible - Sol Ring accelerates everything. This is not a clear blunder.",
      "action_taken": "Put Sol Ring on top of library (to be drawn next), with Puresteel Paladin below it",
      "better_line": "Putting Puresteel Paladin on top is arguably better since the hand already has mana-producing enchantments (Abundant Growth, Fertile Ground) and Puresteel Paladin synergizes powerfully with the Argentum Armor in hand, but Sol Ring on top is defensible for raw acceleration",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 40,
      "player": "GLM47 Grudge",
      "decision_index": 35,
    },
