      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "As part of Brainstorm resolution, GLM47 is putting a card back on top of their library. They chose Terramorphic Expanse, but they have Azorius Chancery in hand which is a tapped land that bounces a land - less immediately useful. More importantly, they should consider putting back their worst cards. With only 2 lands in play (both tapped), they need to develop mana. Terramorphic Expanse is actually a reasonable land to put back since it can be drawn and played to fix mana/thin the deck. However, putting back Argentum Armor (a 6-mana equipment with 6 equip cost - extremely expensive and uncastable for many turns) would be better, as it's a dead card for the foreseeable future. They still need to put back a second card after this one, so context matters, but Terramorphic Expanse is a playable land they may want soon whereas Argentum Armor is nearly unplayable in the early game.",
