    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "GPT5m Romance chose to activate Mind Stone (presumably to sacrifice it and draw a card) during their precombat main phase instead of playing the Swamp from hand first. They have a Swamp in hand and should play their land drop before spending mana on other actions. Additionally, with 6 mana available (Island, Silverbluff Bridge, Mountain, Mind Stone, Oblivion Stone could be tapped but Commander's Sphere too), they could potentially cast Padeem, Consul of Innovation (3U) this turn if they play the Swamp first and use their mana efficiently. Sacrificing Mind Stone for a card draw when you have powerful 4-drops to cast seems like it wastes a mana source prematurely. Playing Swamp first and then casting Padeem (using Island + Silverbluff Bridge for U, Mind Stone for C, Commander's Sphere for U = 3U) would develop a meaningful threat that gives artifacts hexproof and draws cards.",
