    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With 5 lands and 8 cards in hand (likely exceeding the 7-card maximum hand size at end of turn), casting Sol Ring is fine but the sequencing could be better. Sol Ring costs 1 mana, but more importantly, the player should consider what they want to deploy this turn. With Sol Ring providing 2 colorless mana, they could potentially cast more spells. However, the real issue is that they have Abundant Growth and Fertile Ground which are land enchantments that cantrip or ramp - casting Abundant Growth first (costs G) draws a card and fixes mana, and Fertile Ground (costs 1G) ramps. Given they'll need to discard to hand size, they should prioritize deploying as many permanents as possible. Sol Ring is a strong play, but casting Abundant Growth on a land first (to draw a card and potentially find a land or see more options) before committing to Sol Ring would have been slightly better sequencing since they're going to overflow on hand size regardless.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Sol Ring",
      "better_line": "Cast Abundant Growth first (on Exotic Orchard or Forest) to draw a card and potentially enable more plays, then cast Sol Ring with remaining mana, then potentially cast Fertile Ground or Ebony Fly to deploy more permanents before discarding to hand size.",
      "type": "blunder",
