      "decision_index": 523,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Gem3F Optim has 7 Angel tokens (4/4 flyers) and a Manifest creature on the battlefield. GLM47 Grudge is at 15 life with all lands tapped and no creatures. KimiK2 Hothead is at 15 life with all lands tapped and no creatures. GPT5m Romance is already eliminated at -1 life. Attacking with all 7 Angel tokens (28 flying damage) would be lethal against either remaining opponent, and splitting attacks could kill both opponents simultaneously (e.g., 4 Angels at one player for 16 damage and 3 Angels at the other for 12, or any combination that deals 15+ to each). Both opponents have no blockers and are tapped out. This was a missed lethal opportunity to win the game.",
      "action_taken": "Gem3F Optim skipped the attack phase entirely, sending no creatures to attack.",
      "better_line": "Attack GLM47 Grudge with 4 Angel tokens (16 damage, lethal against 15 life) and KimiK2 Hothead with 4 Angel tokens (16 damage, lethal against 15 life) to win the game on the spot. Even attacking all at one player guarantees killing at least one opponent.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 393,
      "player": "Gem3F Optim",
      "decision_index": 526,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "KimiK2 has no creatures on the battlefield, making Tyrite Sanctum's activated abilities completely useless. Arch of Orazca would provide the same colorless mana plus a card draw ability once city's blessing is achieved (they control 8 permanents, need 10). The reasoning incorrectly references a Metalwork Colossus that isn't in play.",
